# AI Provider

The playground spawns **Claude Code** (`claude`) as a subprocess. There is a single provider — `ProviderId` is `'claude-code'`.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `types.ts` | `ProviderId`, `ProviderConfig`, `AgentSpawnOptions`, `ClaudeCodeOptions` |
| `claude-code.ts` | Claude Code CLI config — args, fallback models, options |
| `registry.ts` | `getProvider()`, `DEFAULT_PROVIDER_ID` |
| `spawn-agent.ts` | Process spawn — stdin prompt, SIGTERM cancel |
| `index.ts` | Barrel exports |

## How Generation Works

1. User submits from the docked chat (Edit / Explore / freeform)
2. `POST /playground/api/generate` with the prompt and Claude options
3. `spawn-agent.ts` runs `claude` with the assembled args, pipes the prompt via stdin
4. Agent writes iteration files; the server streams events back to the canvas

